From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - pad GCM decryption data without the ICV

A GCM or CCM decryption chunk ends with the ICV, which SPU-M receives
after the padded data. The driver pads CCM data without the ICV, but
GCM data with it, and sizes the padding in the response without it.
With a 16-byte ICV the two agree. With an 8 or 12-byte ICV the SPU
returns a response of a different length than the buffers given to
the PDC, so the driver reads the status from the wrong place:

  alg: aead: gcm-aes-esp-iproc decryption unexpectedly succeeded on
  test vector "random: alen=16 plen=1040 authsize=8 klen=36
  novrfy=1"; expected_error=-EBADMSG or -22, ...

When the response is shorter, its last receive descriptor is never
written, and the request completes only when the response to another
request arrives. The self-test then waits for it forever.

Pad the data of all GCM and CCM decryptions without the ICV.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 16 +++++-----------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -1426,9 +1426,12 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 	aead_parms.aad_pad_len = spu->spu_gcm_ccm_pad_len(ctx->cipher.mode,
 						 aead_parms.assoc_size);
 
-	/* General case data padding (CCM decrypt special case below) */
+	/*
+	 * General case data padding (RFC4543 special case below), without
+	 * the size of the ICV tacked on to the end of a decryption chunk
+	 */
 	aead_parms.data_pad_len = spu->spu_gcm_ccm_pad_len(ctx->cipher.mode,
-							   chunksize);
+							   datalen);
 
 	if (ctx->cipher.mode == CIPHER_MODE_CCM) {
 		/*
@@ -1439,15 +1442,6 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 					 ctx->cipher.mode,
 					 aead_parms.assoc_size + 2);
 
-		/*
-		 * And when decrypting CCM, need to pad without including
-		 * size of ICV which is tacked on to end of chunk
-		 */
-		if (!rctx->is_encrypt)
-			aead_parms.data_pad_len =
-				spu->spu_gcm_ccm_pad_len(ctx->cipher.mode,
-							chunksize - digestsize);
-
 		/* CCM also requires software to rewrite portions of IV: */
 		spu->spu_ccm_update_iv(digestsize, &cipher_parms, req->assoclen,
 				       chunksize, rctx->is_encrypt,
